<p>Business owners and property managers looking for <strong>roofing contractors in Temple, TX</strong> usually need two things: a clear picture of what is wrong with the roof, and a plan that keeps the building operating while the work gets done. Temple Roofers handles commercial roofing for retail buildings, offices, warehouses, churches, and multi-unit properties throughout Temple and the surrounding Bell County communities. We work on low-slope membrane roofs, modified bitumen, and metal roof systems, and we put our findings in writing with photos so decision-makers can review them without a site visit.</p>

<h2>Common Commercial Roof Problems</h2>
<p>Low-slope roofs fail differently than sloped residential roofs. Water moves slowly, seams carry much of the load, and small defects can travel a long way before showing up inside. Signs that call for a professional look include:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Ponding water</strong> that remains on the roof well after a rain has ended</li>
<li>Ceiling tile stains, drips near light fixtures, or musty odors in upper floors</li>
