<h2>Ponding Water and Drainage</h2>
<p>"Flat" roofs are rarely truly flat; they are designed with a slight slope toward drains, scuppers or gutters. When that drainage is blocked or the deck has settled, water collects in low spots. Standing water adds weight, accelerates membrane aging, and can find its way into any small seam defect. Common fixes include clearing and resizing drains, adding tapered insulation to redirect flow, installing crickets behind rooftop units and chimneys, and upgrading undersized scuppers and downspouts. Our <a href="/services/gutters-roof-drainage-temple-tx/">gutters and roof drainage</a> service covers the edge-of-roof side of this work.</p>

